+## Sales and variance
+
+`POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+`ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` an ISO instant, `qty` a whole number)
+and answers `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: the new tickets imported and the
+dishes sold in them (the sum of `qty`). Tickets already imported are skipped.
+If a row is invalid (`bad_request`) or an item runs out
+(`import_not_enough_stock`, 409), nothing is imported and the message names
+the row (`row 2` is the first data row).
+
+`GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` answers one line per
+item `{ itemId, name, unit, theoretical, actual, difference }`, where
+`difference` is `actual - theoretical`.
